{"id":"chatcmpl-d593a77d-6ff4-441e-940d-f1db99bdae22","object":"chat.completion","created":1795245491,"model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","reasoning_content":"","content":"```json\n{\n  \"highlights\": \"This task resolves a binary laterality question (left vs right) about a radiological finding by combining a descriptive expert query with localization/grounding tools. The key strategy is to first ask for a targeted description, then use grounding to confirm spatial laterality when the description is ambiguous or negative. The final answer is validated by matching the localized region to the correct option.\",\n  \"patterns\": [\n    \"When options differ only by laterality (left vs right), explicitly ask the expert tool to specify laterality rather than just presence/absence.\",\n    \"If a descriptive report returns no focal finding, escalate to a grounding/localization tool to directly test each candidate option's spatial plausibility.\",\n    \"Use phrase-grounding on each candidate answer to confirm whether the described finding can be localized to the expected anatomical region.\",\n    \"Resolve ambiguity by mapping the grounded image region (e.g., image-right = patient-left) to the correct option label.\"\n  ],\n  \"playbooks\": {\n    \"Radiology multiple-choice\": \"Ask targeted descriptive questions that disambiguate the exact option dimension (laterality, location, severity). Fall back to grounding tools when descriptions are inconclusive.\",\n    \"Binary laterality questions\": \"Query each candidate phrase separately through a grounding tool and select the one that localizes to a plausible anatomical region.\",\n    \"Tool-chaining under uncertainty\": \"Sequence: descriptive expert -> grounded report -> phrase grounding on candidates -> answer; stop early if a tool gives a definitive localization.\"\n  },\n  \"checklists\": [\n    \"Confirm the distinguishing dimension between options (e.g., laterality) and ensure the expert query explicitly requests it.\",\n    \"Verify the grounded region's anatomical side matches the chosen option (account for image-left vs patient-right conventions).\"\n  ]\n}\n```"},"finish_reason":"stop","logprobs":null}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":487,"total_tokens":860,"completion_tokens":373,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"image_tokens":0,"text_tokens":487},"completion_tokens_details":{"text_tokens":373}}}